---
title: How to Automate a Workflow for “Conversation Delete” in Taskip
sidebar:
  order: 13
---
**This workflow helps you automatically delete conversations based on specific conditions keeping your inbox clean and focused on what matters most.**

### **Step 1: Open Workflow Settings**

1. **From the left sidebar, go to Workflow.**
1. **Click the + Create Workflow button in the top-right corner.**

*Taskip workflow*

### **Step 2: Name and Choose Trigger**

1. **Give your workflow a meaningful name, like:**
   - **“Delete Auto Replies”**
   - **“Clear Spam Conversations”**
1. **Under the Inbox tab, select this trigger: Conversation Delete\
   *“Move conversations sent from person, address or number”***

***This is the last option in the trigger list, shown on the right in your screenshot.***

### **Step 3: Define the Conditions (IF)**

**Use conditions to tell Taskip when to delete a conversation.**

**Examples:**

- **Subject contains “Out of Office”**
- **Sender email is `noreply@domain.com`**
- **Message body contains “auto-reply” or “delivery failure”**

**You can combine multiple conditions using + Add Condition to fine-tune the rule.**

### **Step 4: Action = Auto Delete**

**The action for this trigger is built-in: Delete Conversation\
You don’t need to add extra steps here once the condition is met, the conversation will be removed automatically.**

### **Step 5: Save the Workflow**

- **Click Create Workflow to save it.**
- **Your automation will now be listed on the Workflow dashboard.**
- **Make sure the status is set to Active.**

### **Example Use Case**

> ***Workflow Name: Auto-Delete No-Reply Emails\
Condition: Sender email is `noreply@notifications.com`\
Result: Deletes all system-generated emails automatically***
